1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,304
My driver's license has a stranger's face on it. And that stranger is currently driving the car I am sitting in.

2
00:00:08,604 --> 00:00:17,052
My name is Eli. I hitched a ride twenty miles back to escape the storm, stepping into this silent, rusted sedan.

3
00:00:17,352 --> 00:00:25,488
The driver hasn't spoken a word. His knuckles are white on the steering wheel, his eyes fixed relentlessly on the road.

4
00:00:25,788 --> 00:00:31,980
When he reached for his coffee, his wallet fell open. I picked it up to hand it back, but stopped cold.

5
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:41,136
The ID lists my name, my birthdate, and my home address. But the face staring back is his hollow, aging features.

6
00:00:41,436 --> 00:00:48,924
Panic shatters my composure. I reach for the door handle, but the child locks click shut with a deafening thud.

7
00:00:49,224 --> 00:00:57,552
He finally turns to look at me, his voice barely a whisper. "You always try to jump out right at mile fifty-two."

8
00:00:57,852 --> 00:01:06,084
He pulls over. He hands me a silver pocket watch engraved with my mother's initials—the one I lost three years ago.

9
00:01:06,384 --> 00:01:14,280
He isn't a kidnapper. He is me, forty years from now, driven to replay the night I ran away from home.

10
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:21,852
He smiles sadly and unlocks the door. "If you step out now, will your driver's license keep your face?"
